Pathfind database migrations — managed by Alembic.

## Common commands (run from the project root)

  # Generate a new auto-migration after changing models.py
  alembic -c backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "describe your change"

  # Apply all pending migrations
  alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head

  # Roll back the most recent migration
  alembic -c backend/alembic.ini downgrade -1

  # Show current migration state
  alembic -c backend/alembic.ini current

  # Show full migration history
  alembic -c backend/alembic.ini history

## Environment variables

  DATABASE_URL   — overrides the sqlalchemy.url in alembic.ini
                   e.g. postgresql://pathfind:secret@localhost:5432/pathfind

## Docker / ECS

  The Dockerfile entrypoint runs Uvicorn directly. For production deployments,
  run migrations as a one-off task BEFORE updating the ECS service:

    alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head
